module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedBasis
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.PolynomialLift
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.SquareZeroDerivation
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.SquareZeroLiftData

/-! # The kernel of a reduction of graded divided power polynomial algebras

Let `q : R' → R` be a surjection of commutative rings whose kernel is the principal ideal
generated by `f : R'`, let `A` be a graded divided power polynomial algebra over `R[xᵢ]` and let
`B` be one over `R'[xᵢ]` with the *same* variables in each degree. A ring morphism `π : B → A`
carrying the coefficients to the coefficients along `q`, matching up the variables, preserving
degrees and preserving divided powers is then nothing but coefficientwise reduction along `q` in
the two monomial bases of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/GradedBasis.lean`. This file reads off the
two consequences of that which Tag 09PS needs:

* the kernel of `π` is exactly `f · B`, and
* the comparison map `κ : ker π → A/IA` of
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift` exists, where `I` is the image under `q` of
  the annihilator of `f`.

These are the clauses `mem_ker_iff` and `kappa_apply` of
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift`, and they are the only two that need freeness —
the remaining clauses are statements about the structure maps and the differential and are proved
without any basis.

## Main definitions

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction` — the comparison data between two
  graded divided power polynomial presentations over a surjection of base rings: the morphism,
  the degreewise bijection of variables, and the four compatibilities.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.variableEquiv` and
  `exponentEquiv` — the induced bijections of variables and of exponent vectors.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.reduceCoeff` — the coefficient family
  of `A` attached to one of `B`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.kappa` — the comparison map `κ`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftCoefficientAlgHom` — the coefficient map of the lifted
  algebra of
  `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/SquareZeroLiftData.lean`, as an
  `R'`-algebra morphism out of `R'[xᵢ]`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftReduction` — that lift, as a reduction, given a polynomial
  presentation of it whose variables are the lifted variables.

## Main results

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.map_monomial` — `π` carries the
  monomial attached to an exponent vector to the monomial attached to the transported exponent
  vector. This is the index-for-index match of the two monomial bases.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.map_coefficient_eq_zero` — linear
  independence of the monomials of `A`, read as a statement about a coefficient family of `B`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.map_eq_zero_iff` — the kernel of `π`
  is `f · B`. This is the clause `mem_ker_iff` of
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.map_mem_annihilatorSMul` — an element
  of `B` killed by `f` has image in `I · A`. This is what makes `κ` well defined.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction.kappa_apply` — `κ` sends `f · b` to
  the class of `π b`. This is the clause `kappa_apply` of
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftRingHom_eq_zero_iff` and
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftKappa_apply` — the same two clauses for the lift of
  `SquareZeroLiftData.lean`.

## Implementation notes

The two clauses are proved from polynomial *presentations* of both algebras rather than from the
tower that builds the lift. That is where the freeness lives: a presentation is what the monomial
basis of `GradedBasis.lean` is stated for. The four comparison fields of
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.GradedPolynomialReduction` are, for the lift, exactly
`liftRingHom_coefficient`, `liftRingHom_variable`, `liftHom_mem_grade` and `liftHom_dpow`, so
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftReduction` takes only a presentation as a hypothesis.

The linear order on the variables that the monomials are formed with is *not* chosen
independently on the two sides: a monomial is an ordered product, so an order on the variables of
`B` transported from one on the variables of `A` is what makes the two monomial bases correspond
index for index rather than up to a sign. The statements that mention a monomial therefore carry
both orders together with the hypothesis that the bijection of variables is strictly monotone,
and the statements that do not — the two clauses themselves — pick an order internally, by
well-ordering the variables of `B` and pulling it back.

The homogeneous case comes first in both proofs and the general case is reduced to it by
decomposing: `f · B` is a graded submodule, because `f` has degree zero, so a vanishing image or
a vanishing product with `f` is inherited by every homogeneous component.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

namespace DividedPowers.TateResolution

universe u v w x z

/-- A monomial of a graded divided power polynomial algebra commutes with a coefficient: the
coefficients sit in degree zero, so the Koszul sign is trivial. -/
public theorem GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomial_mul_coefficient_comm
    {R : Type u} {P : Type v} {A : Type w}
    [CommRing R] [Ring P] [Algebra R P] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    {Aᵢ : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra Aᵢ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm Aᵢ]
    {γ : DividedPowerStructure Aᵢ} {ι : P →ₐ[R] A}
    (G : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial Aᵢ γ ι) [LinearOrder G.Variable]
    {ν : G.Variable →₀ ℕ} (hν : G.IsAdmissible ν) (p : P) :
    G.monomial ν * ι p = ι p * G.monomial ν := by
  rw [IsStrictlyGradedComm.graded_comm (R := R) (G.coefficient_mem p)
    (GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomial_mem_grade hν), Nat.zero_mul, pow_zero, one_smul]

/-- The comparison data making a graded divided power polynomial algebra `B` over `R'[xᵢ]` a
*reduction* of one, `A`, over `R[xᵢ]` along a morphism `q : R' → R` of base rings: a ring
morphism `π : B → A`, a bijection between the variables of the two in each degree, and the four
compatibilities — `π` reduces coefficients along `q`, matches up the variables, preserves
homogeneous degrees, and preserves divided powers.

This is the data under which the kernel of `π` can be computed. The two base rings are *not*
assumed related beyond the morphism `q`; the hypotheses that make the kernel principal — that `q`
is surjective with kernel `(f)` — are taken where they are used. -/
public structure GradedPolynomialReduction
    {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {B : Type x} {σ : Type z}
    [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
    (q : R' →+* R)
    {𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [IsStrictlyGradedComm 𝒜]
    {γ : DividedPowerStructure 𝒜} {ι : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] A}
    {ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B} [GradedAlgebra ℬ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm ℬ]
    {δ : DividedPowerStructure ℬ} {ι' : MvPolynomial σ R' →ₐ[R'] B}
    (GA : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial 𝒜 γ ι)
    (GB : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial ℬ δ ι') where
  /-- The comparison morphism. -/
  map : B →+* A
  /-- The variables of the two algebras correspond in each degree. -/
  index : ∀ n : ℕ, GA.indices n ≃ GB.indices n
  /-- The comparison morphism reduces coefficients along `q`. -/
  map_coefficient : ∀ p : MvPolynomial σ R', map (ι' p) = ι (MvPolynomial.map q p)
  /-- The comparison morphism matches up the variables. -/
  map_generator : ∀ (n : ℕ) (j : GA.indices n),
    map (GB.generator ⟨n, index n j⟩) = GA.generator ⟨n, j⟩
  /-- The comparison morphism preserves homogeneous degrees. -/
  map_mem_grade : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ n → map b ∈ 𝒜 n
  /-- The comparison morphism preserves divided powers. -/
  map_dpow : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ positiveEvenPart ℬ → map (δ.dpow n b) = γ.dpow n (map b)

namespace GradedPolynomialReduction

section Reduction

variable {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {B : Type x} {σ : Type z}
  [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A] [Ring B] [Algebra R' B]
  {q : R' →+* R} {f : R'}
  {𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [IsStrictlyGradedComm 𝒜]
  {γ : DividedPowerStructure 𝒜} {ι : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] A}
  {ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B} [GradedAlgebra ℬ] [IsStrictlyGradedComm ℬ]
  {δ : DividedPowerStructure ℬ} {ι' : MvPolynomial σ R' →ₐ[R'] B}
  {GA : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial 𝒜 γ ι}
  {GB : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial ℬ δ ι'}
  (h : GradedPolynomialReduction q GA GB)

/-! ### The induced bijections of variables and of exponent vectors -/

/-- The bijection between the variables of the two algebras, assembled from the degreewise
bijections. -/
public def variableEquiv : GA.Variable ≃ GB.Variable := Equiv.sigmaCongrRight h.index

/-- The bijection of variables preserves the degree of a variable. -/
@[simp]
public theorem variableEquiv_fst (j : GA.Variable) : (h.variableEquiv j).1 = j.1 := rfl

/-- Corresponding variables have the same degree. -/
public theorem varDegree_variableEquiv (j : GA.Variable) :
    GB.varDegree (h.variableEquiv j) = GA.varDegree j := rfl

/-- The comparison morphism matches up the variables, indexed as variables rather than by their
degree and index separately. -/
public theorem map_generator_variableEquiv (j : GA.Variable) :
    h.map (GB.generator (h.variableEquiv j)) = GA.generator j :=
  h.map_generator j.1 j.2

/-- The bijection between the exponent vectors of the two algebras. -/
public def exponentEquiv : (GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) ≃ (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) :=
  Finsupp.equivCongrLeft h.variableEquiv

/-- The transported exponent vector takes at the variable corresponding to `j` the value the
original takes at `j`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem exponentEquiv_apply (ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) (j : GA.Variable) :
    h.exponentEquiv ν (h.variableEquiv j) = ν j := by
  simp [exponentEquiv, Finsupp.equivCongrLeft]

/-- Transporting an exponent vector transports its support. -/
public theorem support_exponentEquiv (ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) :
    (h.exponentEquiv ν).support = ν.support.map h.variableEquiv.toEmbedding := rfl

/-- The transport of exponent vectors is reindexing along the bijection of variables. -/
public theorem exponentEquiv_eq (ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) :
    h.exponentEquiv ν = Finsupp.equivMapDomain h.variableEquiv ν := rfl

/-- Transporting an exponent vector preserves its weight: corresponding variables have the same
degree. -/
public theorem weight_exponentEquiv (ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) :
    GB.weight (h.exponentEquiv ν) = GA.weight ν := by
  rw [GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.weight, GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.weight,
    exponentEquiv_eq, Finsupp.equivMapDomain_eq_mapDomain,
    Finsupp.sum_mapDomain_index_inj h.variableEquiv.injective]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ =>
    congrArg (fun d => ν j * d) (h.varDegree_variableEquiv j)

/-- Transporting an exponent vector preserves admissibility. -/
public theorem isAdmissible_exponentEquiv {ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ} (hν : GA.IsAdmissible ν) :
    GB.IsAdmissible (h.exponentEquiv ν) := by
  intro i hi
  obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := h.variableEquiv.surjective i
  rw [exponentEquiv_apply]
  exact hν j (h.varDegree_variableEquiv j ▸ hi)

/-- Transporting an exponent vector of a monomial of degree `n` gives one of degree `n`. -/
public theorem mem_monomialSet_exponentEquiv {n : ℕ} {ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ}
    (hν : ν ∈ GA.monomialSet n) : h.exponentEquiv ν ∈ GB.monomialSet n :=
  ⟨h.isAdmissible_exponentEquiv hν.1, by rw [weight_exponentEquiv, hν.2]⟩

/-- Transporting back an exponent vector of a monomial of degree `n` gives one of degree `n`. -/
public theorem mem_monomialSet_of_exponentEquiv {n : ℕ} {μ : GB.Variable →₀ ℕ}
    (hμ : μ ∈ GB.monomialSet n) : h.exponentEquiv.symm μ ∈ GA.monomialSet n := by
  refine ⟨fun j hj => ?_, ?_⟩
  · have := hμ.1 (h.variableEquiv j) ((h.varDegree_variableEquiv j).symm ▸ hj)
    rwa [show h.exponentEquiv.symm μ j = μ (h.variableEquiv j) from by
      rw [← exponentEquiv_apply h (h.exponentEquiv.symm μ) j, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]]
  · rw [← h.weight_exponentEquiv (h.exponentEquiv.symm μ), Equiv.apply_symm_apply, hμ.2]

/-- Transporting the zero exponent vector gives the zero exponent vector. -/
@[simp]
public theorem exponentEquiv_zero : h.exponentEquiv 0 = 0 := by
  refine Finsupp.ext fun y => ?_
  obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := h.variableEquiv.surjective y
  rw [exponentEquiv_apply]
  rfl

/-- Transporting an exponent vector commutes with erasing a variable. -/
public theorem exponentEquiv_erase (ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) (j : GA.Variable) :
    h.exponentEquiv (ν.erase j) = (h.exponentEquiv ν).erase (h.variableEquiv j) := by
  refine Finsupp.ext fun y => ?_
  obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := h.variableEquiv.surjective y
  by_cases hij : i = j
  · subst hij
    rw [exponentEquiv_apply, Finsupp.erase_same, Finsupp.erase_same]
  · rw [exponentEquiv_apply, Finsupp.erase_ne hij,
      Finsupp.erase_ne (fun hc => hij (h.variableEquiv.injective hc)), exponentEquiv_apply]

/-! ### The two monomial bases correspond index for index -/

/-- The comparison morphism carries each divided power of a variable of `B` to the corresponding
divided power of the corresponding variable of `A`. In odd degree both are ordinary powers; in
even degree this is where `π` being a morphism of divided powers is used. -/
public theorem map_variablePower (j : GA.Variable) (k : ℕ) :
    h.map (GB.variablePower (h.variableEquiv j) k) = GA.variablePower j k := by
  rw [GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.variablePower, GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.variablePower,
    h.varDegree_variableEquiv j]
  split_ifs with hodd
  · rw [map_pow, h.map_generator_variableEquiv]
  · rw [h.map_dpow k _ (GB.generator_mem_positiveEvenPart
      ((h.varDegree_variableEquiv j).symm ▸ Nat.not_odd_iff_even.1 hodd)),
      h.map_generator_variableEquiv]

/-- **The two monomial bases correspond.** The comparison morphism carries the monomial of `B`
attached to a transported exponent vector to the monomial of `A` attached to that exponent
vector, provided the order on the variables of `B` is such that the bijection of variables is
strictly monotone — the two monomials are then products of corresponding factors in corresponding
orders. -/
public theorem map_monomial [LinearOrder GA.Variable] [LinearOrder GB.Variable]
    (hmono : StrictMono h.variableEquiv) (ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) :
    h.map (GB.monomial (h.exponentEquiv ν)) = GA.monomial ν := by
  classical
  have hempty : ∀ μ : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ, μ.support = ∅ →
      h.map (GB.monomial (h.exponentEquiv μ)) = GA.monomial μ := by simp +contextual
  suffices hall : ∀ (c : ℕ) (μ : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ), μ.support.card ≤ c →
      h.map (GB.monomial (h.exponentEquiv μ)) = GA.monomial μ from hall ν.support.card ν le_rfl
  intro c
  induction c with
  | zero =>
    intro μ hc
    exact hempty μ (by simpa using hc)
  | succ c ih =>
    intro μ hc
    rcases μ.support.eq_empty_or_nonempty with he | hne
    · exact hempty μ he
    · set j := μ.support.min' hne with hjdef
      have hjmem : j ∈ μ.support := Finset.min'_mem _ hne
      have hlt : ∀ x ∈ μ.support, x ≠ j → j < x := fun x hx hxj =>
        lt_of_le_of_ne (Finset.min'_le _ _ hx) (Ne.symm hxj)
      have hltB : ∀ y ∈ (h.exponentEquiv μ).support, y ≠ h.variableEquiv j →
          h.variableEquiv j < y := by
        intro y hy hyj
        rw [h.support_exponentEquiv] at hy
        obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_map.1 hy
        exact hmono (hlt x hx fun hc' => hyj (by rw [hc']; rfl))
      have hcard : (μ.erase j).support.card ≤ c := by
        rw [Finsupp.support_erase]
        have := Finset.card_erase_of_mem hjmem
        omega
      rw [GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomial_erase (h.exponentEquiv μ) (h.variableEquiv j) hltB,
        GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomial_erase μ j hlt, map_mul, ← h.exponentEquiv_erase,
        ih _ hcard, h.exponentEquiv_apply, h.map_variablePower]

/-! ### Coefficientwise reduction -/

/-- The coefficient family of `A` attached to one of `B`: the coefficients are reduced along `q`
and the monomials reindexed along the bijection of variables. -/
public def reduceCoeff (c : (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R') :
    (GA.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R :=
  Finsupp.mapDomain h.exponentEquiv.symm
    (Finsupp.mapRange (MvPolynomial.map q) (map_zero (MvPolynomial.map q)) c)

/-- The attached coefficient family of `A` at the exponent vector corresponding to `μ` is the
reduction along `q` of the coefficient of `B` at `μ`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem reduceCoeff_apply (c : (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R')
    (μ : GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) :
    h.reduceCoeff c (h.exponentEquiv.symm μ) = MvPolynomial.map q (c μ) := by
  rw [reduceCoeff, Finsupp.mapDomain_apply_of_injective h.exponentEquiv.symm.injective,
    Finsupp.mapRange_apply]

/-- The attached coefficient family of `A` is supported on the monomials of the same degree. -/
public theorem mem_monomialSet_of_mem_support_reduceCoeff {n : ℕ}
    {c : (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R'}
    (hc : ∀ μ ∈ c.support, μ ∈ GB.monomialSet n) {ν : GA.Variable →₀ ℕ}
    (hν : ν ∈ (h.reduceCoeff c).support) : ν ∈ GA.monomialSet n := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 (Finsupp.mapDomain_support hν)
  exact h.mem_monomialSet_of_exponentEquiv (hc μ (Finsupp.support_mapRange hμ))

/-- The comparison morphism is coefficientwise reduction in the two monomial bases. -/
public theorem map_monomialSumMap [LinearOrder GA.Variable] [LinearOrder GB.Variable]
    (hmono : StrictMono h.variableEquiv) (c : (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R') :
    h.map (GB.monomialSumMap c) = GA.monomialSumMap (h.reduceCoeff c) := by
  rw [GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomialSumMap_apply,
    GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomialSumMap_apply, reduceCoeff,
    Finsupp.sum_mapDomain_index_inj h.exponentEquiv.symm.injective,
    Finsupp.sum_mapRange_index (fun _ => by simp), Finsupp.sum, Finsupp.sum, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun μ _ => ?_
  rw [map_mul, h.map_coefficient, ← h.map_monomial hmono (h.exponentEquiv.symm μ),
    Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- Coefficientwise reduction, expanded as a sum over the support of the coefficient family of
`B`. -/
public theorem map_monomialSumMap_sum [LinearOrder GA.Variable] [LinearOrder GB.Variable]
    (hmono : StrictMono h.variableEquiv) (c : (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R') :
    h.map (GB.monomialSumMap c) =
      ∑ μ ∈ c.support,
        GA.monomial (h.exponentEquiv.symm μ) * ι (MvPolynomial.map q (c μ)) := by
  rw [h.map_monomialSumMap hmono, GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomialSumMap_apply, reduceCoeff,
    Finsupp.sum_mapDomain_index_inj h.exponentEquiv.symm.injective,
    Finsupp.sum_mapRange_index (by simp), Finsupp.sum]

/-- Linear independence of the monomials of `A`, read as a statement about a coefficient family
of `B`: if a combination of the monomials of `B` of degree `n` is killed by the comparison
morphism, then every coefficient is killed by `q`. -/
public theorem map_coefficient_eq_zero [LinearOrder GA.Variable] [LinearOrder GB.Variable]
    (hmono : StrictMono h.variableEquiv) {n : ℕ}
    {c : (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R'}
    (hc : ∀ μ ∈ c.support, μ ∈ GB.monomialSet n)
    (h0 : h.map (GB.monomialSumMap c) = 0) (μ : GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) :
    MvPolynomial.map q (c μ) = 0 := by
  rw [h.map_monomialSumMap hmono] at h0
  have hz := GA.eq_zero_of_monomialSumMap_eq_zero_of_mem_monomialSet n (h.reduceCoeff c)
    (fun _ hν => h.mem_monomialSet_of_mem_support_reduceCoeff hc hν) h0
  rw [← h.reduceCoeff_apply c μ, hz, Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply]

/-! ### The kernel of the comparison morphism -/

/-- The generator of the kernel of `q` is killed by the comparison morphism. -/
public theorem map_algebraMap_eq_zero (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) :
    h.map (algebraMap R' B f) = 0 := by
  have hqf : q f = 0 :=
    RingHom.mem_ker.1 (by rw [hf]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self f)
  rw [show algebraMap R' B f = ι' (MvPolynomial.C f) from (MvPolynomial.algHom_C ι' f).symm,
    h.map_coefficient, MvPolynomial.map_C, hqf, MvPolynomial.C_0, map_zero]

/-- A homogeneous element killed by the comparison morphism is a multiple of the generator of the
kernel of `q`: each of its coefficients is killed by `q`, hence divisible by that generator, and
the quotients reassemble. -/
public theorem exists_eq_generator_mul_of_mem_grade (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f})
    {n : ℕ} {b : B} (hb : b ∈ ℬ n) (h0 : h.map b = 0) :
    ∃ c : B, b = algebraMap R' B f * c := by
  classical
  let _ : LinearOrder GB.Variable := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let _ : LinearOrder GA.Variable := LinearOrder.lift' h.variableEquiv h.variableEquiv.injective
  have hmono : StrictMono h.variableEquiv := fun _ _ hab => hab
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hcb⟩ := GB.exists_monomialSumMap_eq n hb
  have hzero : ∀ μ, MvPolynomial.map q (c μ) = 0 :=
    h.map_coefficient_eq_zero hmono hc (by rw [hcb]; exact h0)
  have hdiv : ∀ μ, ∃ d, c μ = MvPolynomial.C f * d := fun μ =>
    exists_eq_C_mul_of_map_eq_zero q f hf (c μ) (hzero μ)
  choose d hd using hdiv
  refine ⟨∑ μ ∈ c.support, GB.monomial μ * ι' (d μ), ?_⟩
  rw [← hcb, GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomialSumMap_apply, Finsupp.sum, Finset.mul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun μ _ => ?_
  rw [hd μ, map_mul, MvPolynomial.algHom_C,
    IsSquareZeroLift.generator_mul_comm f (GB.monomial μ) (ι' (d μ))]

/-- The comparison morphism commutes with taking a homogeneous component. -/
public theorem map_decompose (n : ℕ) (b : B) :
    ((DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 (h.map b) n : 𝒜 n) : A) =
      h.map ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : ℬ n) : B) := by
  induction b using DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn ℬ with
  | zero => simp
  | @homogeneous m b =>
      rcases eq_or_ne m n with rfl | hmn
      · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same ℬ b.2,
          DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 (h.map_mem_grade m b b.2)]
      · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne ℬ b.2 hmn,
          DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒜 (h.map_mem_grade m b b.2) hmn, map_zero]
  | add b c hb hc =>
      rw [map_add, DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply, Submodule.coe_add, hb, hc,
        DirectSum.decompose_add, DirectSum.add_apply, Submodule.coe_add, map_add]

/-- **The kernel of the comparison morphism is generated by the generator of the kernel of `q`.**
This is the clause `mem_ker_iff` of `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift`. -/
public theorem map_eq_zero_iff (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) (b : B) :
    h.map b = 0 ↔ ∃ c : B, b = algebraMap R' B f * c := by
  classical
  refine ⟨fun h0 => ?_, fun ⟨c, hc⟩ => by
    rw [hc, map_mul, h.map_algebraMap_eq_zero hf, zero_mul]⟩
  have hcomp : ∀ n : ℕ, h.map ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : ℬ n) : B) = 0 := by
    intro n
    rw [← h.map_decompose n b, h0]
    simp
  have hex : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ c : B,
      ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : ℬ n) : B) = algebraMap R' B f * c := fun n =>
    h.exists_eq_generator_mul_of_mem_grade hf (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n).2 (hcomp n)
  choose cc hcc using hex
  refine ⟨∑ n ∈ (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b).support, cc n, ?_⟩
  have hsum : algebraMap R' B f * ∑ n ∈ (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b).support, cc n =
      ∑ n ∈ (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b).support, ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : ℬ n) : B) := by
    rw [Finset.mul_sum]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ => (hcc n).symm
  rw [hsum, DirectSum.sum_support_decompose ℬ b]

/-! ### The comparison map `κ` -/

/-- A homogeneous element of `B` annihilated by the generator of the kernel of `q` has image in
`I · A`, where `I` is the image under `q` of the annihilator of that generator: every coefficient
of the element annihilates the generator, so every coefficient of its image lies in `I`. -/
public theorem map_mem_annihilatorSMul_of_mem_grade {n : ℕ} {b : B} (hb : b ∈ ℬ n)
    (h0 : algebraMap R' B f * b = 0) :
    h.map b ∈ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A := by
  classical
  let _ : LinearOrder GB.Variable := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let _ : LinearOrder GA.Variable := LinearOrder.lift' h.variableEquiv h.variableEquiv.injective
  have hmono : StrictMono h.variableEquiv := fun _ _ hab => hab
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hcb⟩ := GB.exists_monomialSumMap_eq n hb
  have hstep : GB.monomialSumMap (Finsupp.mapRange
      (fun p : MvPolynomial σ R' => MvPolynomial.C f * p) (mul_zero _) c) =
      algebraMap R' B f * GB.monomialSumMap c := by
    rw [GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomialSumMap_apply,
      GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomialSumMap_apply,
      Finsupp.sum_mapRange_index (fun _ => by simp), Finsupp.sum, Finsupp.sum, Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun μ _ => ?_
    rw [map_mul, MvPolynomial.algHom_C,
      IsSquareZeroLift.generator_mul_comm f (GB.monomial μ) (ι' (c μ))]
  have hvan : Finsupp.mapRange (fun p : MvPolynomial σ R' => MvPolynomial.C f * p)
      (mul_zero _) c = 0 :=
    GB.eq_zero_of_monomialSumMap_eq_zero_of_mem_monomialSet n _
      (fun _ hμ => hc _ (Finsupp.support_mapRange hμ)) (by rw [hstep, hcb, h0])
  have hCf : ∀ μ : GB.Variable →₀ ℕ, MvPolynomial.C f * c μ = 0 := by
    intro μ
    have hμ := congrArg (fun g : (GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) →₀ MvPolynomial σ R' => g μ) hvan
    simpa using hμ
  have hann : ∀ (μ : GB.Variable →₀ ℕ) (ex : σ →₀ ℕ),
      (c μ).coeff ex ∈ (Ideal.span {f}).annihilator := by
    intro μ ex
    refine (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton f _).2 ?_
    have hco := congrArg (fun p : MvPolynomial σ R' => p.coeff ex) (hCf μ)
    rw [MvPolynomial.coeff_C_mul, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_zero, Finsupp.zero_apply] at hco
    rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_comm]
    exact hco
  rw [← hcb, h.map_monomialSumMap_sum hmono]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun μ hμ => ?_
  have hadm : GA.IsAdmissible (h.exponentEquiv.symm μ) :=
    (h.mem_monomialSet_of_exponentEquiv (hc μ hμ)).1
  rw [GradedDividedPowerPolynomial.monomial_mul_coefficient_comm GA hadm]
  refine eval_mul_mem_smul_top _ ι _ (fun ex => ?_) _
  rw [MvPolynomial.coeff_map]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem q (hann μ ex)

/-- An element of `B` annihilated by the generator of the kernel of `q` has image in `I · A`.
This is what makes the comparison map `κ` well defined. -/
public theorem map_mem_annihilatorSMul {b : B} (h0 : algebraMap R' B f * b = 0) :
    h.map b ∈ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A := by
  classical
  have hcomp : ∀ n : ℕ,
      algebraMap R' B f * ((DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n : ℬ n) : B) = 0 := by
    intro n
    have h0' : f • b = 0 := by rwa [Algebra.smul_def]
    rw [← Algebra.smul_def, ← IsSquareZeroLift.decompose_smul_coe ℬ f b n, h0']
    simp
  have hsum := DirectSum.sum_support_decompose ℬ b
  rw [← hsum, map_sum]
  exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun n _ =>
    h.map_mem_annihilatorSMul_of_mem_grade (DirectSum.decompose ℬ b n).2 (hcomp n)

/-- Two cofactors of the same multiple of the generator of the kernel of `q` have the same image
in `A/IA`: their difference is annihilated by that generator. -/
public theorem quotient_mk_map_eq {b b' : B}
    (hbb : algebraMap R' B f * b = algebraMap R' B f * b') :
    (Submodule.Quotient.mk (h.map b) : A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A) =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk (h.map b') := by
  refine (Submodule.Quotient.eq _).2 ?_
  rw [← map_sub]
  exact h.map_mem_annihilatorSMul (by rw [mul_sub, hbb, sub_self])

/-- A chosen cofactor of an element of the kernel of the comparison morphism. -/
public def kerCofactor (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) (ξ : RingHom.ker h.map) : B :=
  ((h.map_eq_zero_iff hf (ξ : B)).1 (RingHom.mem_ker.1 ξ.2)).choose

/-- The chosen cofactor is a cofactor. -/
public theorem generator_mul_kerCofactor (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f})
    (ξ : RingHom.ker h.map) : (ξ : B) = algebraMap R' B f * h.kerCofactor hf ξ :=
  ((h.map_eq_zero_iff hf (ξ : B)).1 (RingHom.mem_ker.1 ξ.2)).choose_spec

/-- **The comparison map `κ` of Tag 09PS**: an element of the kernel of the comparison morphism
is a multiple of the generator of the kernel of `q`, and `κ` sends it to the class of the image of
its cofactor. The cofactor is only determined up to the annihilator of that generator, which is
exactly what the quotient by `I · A` divides out. -/
public def kappa (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) :
    RingHom.ker h.map →+ A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A where
  toFun ξ := Submodule.Quotient.mk (h.map (h.kerCofactor hf ξ))
  map_zero' := by
    have hz : algebraMap R' B f * h.kerCofactor hf 0 = algebraMap R' B f * 0 := by
      rw [mul_zero, ← h.generator_mul_kerCofactor hf 0]
      rfl
    rw [h.quotient_mk_map_eq hz, map_zero]
    simp
  map_add' ξ ξ' := by
    have hz : algebraMap R' B f * h.kerCofactor hf (ξ + ξ') =
        algebraMap R' B f * (h.kerCofactor hf ξ + h.kerCofactor hf ξ') := by
      rw [mul_add, ← h.generator_mul_kerCofactor hf ξ, ← h.generator_mul_kerCofactor hf ξ',
        ← h.generator_mul_kerCofactor hf (ξ + ξ')]
      rfl
    rw [h.quotient_mk_map_eq hz, map_add]
    rfl

/-- **The comparison map sends `f · b` to the class of `π b`.** This is the clause `kappa_apply`
of `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift`. -/
public theorem kappa_apply (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) (b : B)
    (hb : algebraMap R' B f * b ∈ RingHom.ker h.map) :
    h.kappa hf ⟨algebraMap R' B f * b, hb⟩ = Submodule.Quotient.mk (h.map b) := by
  refine h.quotient_mk_map_eq ?_
  rw [← h.generator_mul_kerCofactor hf ⟨algebraMap R' B f * b, hb⟩]

end Reduction

end GradedPolynomialReduction

/-! ### The two clauses for the lift of `SquareZeroLiftData.lean` -/

section Lift

attribute [local instance] GradedDPAlgebra.ring GradedDPAlgebra.algebra
  GradedDPAlgebra.graded GradedDPAlgebra.strict

attribute [local instance] gradedLimitGradedAlgebra gradedLimitStrictlyGradedComm

variable {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {σ : Type z}
  [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
  (q : R' →+* R) {f : R'} {𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [IsStrictlyGradedComm 𝒜]
  {γ : DividedPowerStructure 𝒜} {ι : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] A}
  (hpoly : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial 𝒜 γ ι)

/-- The coefficient map of the lifted algebra `B`, as an `R'`-algebra morphism out of `R'[xᵢ]`:
the inclusion of the base of the tower, read through the identification of that base with
`R'[xᵢ]`. -/
public def liftCoefficientAlgHom :
    MvPolynomial σ R' →ₐ[R'] (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier :=
  (liftCoefficientHom (R' := R') hpoly).hom.comp (liftBaseEquiv R' σ R A).symm.toAlgHom

/-- The lift of `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/SquareZeroLiftData.lean`,
as a reduction. The four comparison fields hold for that lift; the one hypothesis is a polynomial
presentation of the lifted algebra whose variables are the lifted variables. -/
public def liftReduction
    (hpolyB : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).grade
      (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).gamma (liftCoefficientAlgHom (R' := R') hpoly))
    (e : ∀ n : ℕ, hpoly.indices n ≃ hpolyB.indices n)
    (hgen : ∀ (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n),
      hpolyB.generator ⟨n, e n j⟩ = liftVariable (R' := R') hpoly n j) :
    GradedPolynomialReduction q hpoly hpolyB where
  map := liftRingHom q hpoly
  index := e
  map_coefficient := liftRingHom_coefficient q hpoly
  map_generator n j := by rw [hgen n j, liftRingHom_variable]
  map_mem_grade := liftHom_mem_grade q hpoly
  map_dpow n b hb := (liftHom_dpow q hpoly n b hb).symm

/-- **The kernel of `π` is `f · B`, for the lift of `SquareZeroLiftData.lean`.** This is the
clause `mem_ker_iff` of `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift` for that lift. -/
public theorem liftRingHom_eq_zero_iff (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f})
    (hpolyB : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).grade
      (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).gamma (liftCoefficientAlgHom (R' := R') hpoly))
    (e : ∀ n : ℕ, hpoly.indices n ≃ hpolyB.indices n)
    (hgen : ∀ (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n),
      hpolyB.generator ⟨n, e n j⟩ = liftVariable (R' := R') hpoly n j)
    (b : (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier) :
    liftRingHom q hpoly b = 0 ↔
      ∃ c : (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier,
        b = algebraMap R' (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier f * c :=
  (liftReduction q hpoly hpolyB e hgen).map_eq_zero_iff hf b

/-- The comparison map `κ` for the lift of `SquareZeroLiftData.lean`. -/
public def liftKappa (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f})
    (hpolyB : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).grade
      (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).gamma (liftCoefficientAlgHom (R' := R') hpoly))
    (e : ∀ n : ℕ, hpoly.indices n ≃ hpolyB.indices n)
    (hgen : ∀ (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n),
      hpolyB.generator ⟨n, e n j⟩ = liftVariable (R' := R') hpoly n j) :
    RingHom.ker (liftRingHom q hpoly) →+ A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A :=
  (liftReduction q hpoly hpolyB e hgen).kappa hf

/-- **`κ` sends `f · b` to the class of `π b`, for the lift of `SquareZeroLiftData.lean`.** This
is the clause `kappa_apply` of `DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsSquareZeroLift` for that lift. -/
public theorem liftKappa_apply (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f})
    (hpolyB : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).grade
      (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).gamma (liftCoefficientAlgHom (R' := R') hpoly))
    (e : ∀ n : ℕ, hpoly.indices n ≃ hpolyB.indices n)
    (hgen : ∀ (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n),
      hpolyB.generator ⟨n, e n j⟩ = liftVariable (R' := R') hpoly n j)
    (b : (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier)
    (hb : algebraMap R' (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier f * b ∈
      RingHom.ker (liftRingHom q hpoly)) :
    liftKappa q hpoly hf hpolyB e hgen
        ⟨algebraMap R' (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier f * b, hb⟩ =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk (liftRingHom q hpoly b) :=
  (liftReduction q hpoly hpolyB e hgen).kappa_apply hf b hb

end Lift

end DividedPowers.TateResolution

